    "markdown": "![ACL Logo](https://aclanthology.org/images/acl-logo.svg) ACL Anthology ⟨1⟩\n  * About⟨2⟩\n    * Announcements⟨3⟩\n    * Communication channels⟨4⟩\n    * Related work⟨5⟩\n    * Copyright⟨6⟩\n    * * * *\n    * Credits⟨7⟩\n    * Volunteer⟨8⟩\n    * Development⟨9⟩\n    * Feedback⟨10⟩\n  * Using⟨2⟩\n    * Citing papers⟨11⟩\n    * Links in the Anthology⟨12⟩\n    * Data access⟨13⟩\n    * * * *\n    * All FAQs⟨14⟩\n    * * * *\n    * ###### Details\n    * Anthology identifiers⟨15⟩\n    * Names⟨16⟩\n    * ORCID iDs⟨17⟩\n    * DOIs⟨18⟩\n    * Verified authors⟨19⟩\n  * Contributions⟨2⟩\n    * Submissions⟨20⟩\n    * Corrections⟨21⟩\n    * Author pages⟨22⟩\n    * Attachments⟨23⟩\n  * GitHub⟨24⟩\n\n\n## Developing State-Of-The-Art Massively Multilingual Machine Translation Systems for Related Languages⟨25⟩\nJay Gala⟨26⟩, Pranjal A. Chitale⟨27⟩, Raj Dabre⟨28⟩\n##### Correct Metadata for \nUse this form to create a GitHub issue with structured data describing the correction. You will need a GitHub account. Once you create that issue, the correction will be reviewed by a staff member.\n⚠️ Mobile Users: Submitting this form to create a new issue will only work with github.com, not the GitHub Mobile app.\n**Important** : The Anthology treat PDFs as authoritative. Please use this form only to correct data that is out of line with the PDF. See our corrections guidelines⟨21⟩ if you need to change the PDF.\nTitle Adjust the title. Retain tags such as <fixed-case>.\nAuthors Adjust author names and order to match the PDF.Add Author\nAbstract Correct abstract if needed. Retain XML formatting tags such as <tex-math>. You may use <b>...</b> for **bold** , <i>...</i> for _italic_ , <u>...</u> for _underline_ , <sc>...</sc> for small-caps, <tt>...<tt> for `typewriter text`, <url>...</url> for URLs, <a href=...> for hyperlinks, and <par/> for paragraph breaks.\nVerification against PDF Ensure that the new title/authors match the snapshot below. (If there is no snapshot or it is too small, consult the PDF⟨2⟩.)\n![](https://aclanthology.org/2023.ijcnlp-tutorials.6/)⟨2⟩\nAuthors concatenated from the text boxes above:\nALL author names match the snapshot above—including middle initials, hyphens, and accents.\nCreate GitHub issue for staff review\n* * * \n\nAnthology ID:\n    2023.ijcnlp-tutorials.6 \n\nVolume:\n    Proceedings of the 13th International Joint Conference on Natural Language Processing and the 3rd Conference of the Asia-Pacific Chapter of the Association for Computational Linguistics: Tutorial Abstract⟨29⟩ \n\nMonth:\n    November \n\nYear:\n    2023 \n\nAddress:\n    Nusa Dua, Bali \n\nEditors:\n     Yun-Nung (Vivian) Chen⟨30⟩, Sadao Kurohashi⟨31⟩ \n\nVenues:\n     IJCNLP⟨32⟩ | AACL⟨33⟩ \n\nSIG:\n\n\nPublisher:\n    Association for Computational Linguistics \n\nNote:\n\n\nPages:\n    35–42 \n\nLanguage:\n\n\nURL:\n    <https://aclanthology.org/2023.ijcnlp-tutorials.6/> \n\nDOI:\n    10.18653/v1/2023.ijcnlp-tutorials.6⟨34⟩ \n\nBibkey:\n    gala-etal-2023-developing \n\nCite (ACL):\n    Jay Gala, Pranjal A. Chitale, and Raj Dabre. 2023. Developing State-Of-The-Art Massively Multilingual Machine Translation Systems for Related Languages⟨35⟩. In _Proceedings of the 13th International Joint Conference on Natural Language Processing and the 3rd Conference of the Asia-Pacific Chapter of the Association for Computational Linguistics: Tutorial Abstract_ , pages 35–42, Nusa Dua, Bali. Association for Computational Linguistics. \n\nCite (Informal):\n    Developing State-Of-The-Art Massively Multilingual Machine Translation Systems for Related Languages⟨35⟩ (Gala et al., IJCNLP-AACL 2023) \n\nCopy Citation:\n     BibTeX Markdown MODS XML Endnote More options… \n\nPDF:\n    <https://aclanthology.org/2023.ijcnlp-tutorials.6.pdf>\nPDF ⟨25⟩Cite ⟨2⟩Search ⟨36⟩ Fix data⟨2⟩\n* * *\n##### Export citation\n  * BibTeX⟨37⟩\n  * MODS XML⟨38⟩\n  * Endnote⟨39⟩\n  * Preformatted⟨40⟩\n\n\n\n```\n@inproceedings{gala-etal-2023-developing,\n    title = \"Developing State-Of-The-Art Massively Multilingual Machine Translation Systems for Related Languages\",\n    author = \"Gala, Jay  and\n      Chitale, Pranjal A.  and\n      Dabre, Raj\",\n    editor = \"Chen, Yun-Nung (Vivian)  and\n      Kurohashi, Sadao\",\n    booktitle = \"Proceedings of the 13th International Joint Conference on Natural Language Processing and the 3rd Conference of the Asia-Pacific Chapter of the Association for Computational Linguistics: Tutorial Abstract\",\n    month = nov,\n    year = \"2023\",\n    address = \"Nusa Dua, Bali\",\n    publisher = \"Association for Computational Linguistics\",\n    url = \"https://aclanthology.org/2023.ijcnlp-tutorials.6/\",\n    doi = \"10.18653/v1/2023.ijcnlp-tutorials.6\",\n    pages = \"35--42\"\n}\n```\n\nDownload as File Copy to Clipboard\n\n```\n<?xml version=\"1.0\" encoding=\"UTF-8\"?>\n<modsCollection xmlns=\"http://www.loc.gov/mods/v3\">\n<mods ID=\"gala-etal-2023-developing\">\n    <titleInfo>\n        <title>Developing State-Of-The-Art Massively Multilingual Machine Translation Systems for Related Languages</title>\n    </titleInfo>\n    <name type=\"personal\">\n        <namePart type=\"given\">Jay</namePart>\n        <namePart type=\"family\">Gala</namePart>\n        <role>\n            <roleTerm authority=\"marcrelator\" type=\"text\">author</roleTerm>\n        </role>\n    </name>\n    <name type=\"personal\">\n        <namePart type=\"given\">Pranjal</namePart>\n        <namePart type=\"given\">A</namePart>\n        <namePart type=\"family\">Chitale</namePart>\n        <role>\n            <roleTerm authority=\"marcrelator\" type=\"text\">author</roleTerm>\n        </role>\n    </name>\n    <name type=\"personal\">\n        <namePart type=\"given\">Raj</namePart>\n        <namePart type=\"family\">Dabre</namePart>\n        <role>\n            <roleTerm authority=\"marcrelator\" type=\"text\">author</roleTerm>\n        </role>\n    </name>\n    <originInfo>\n        <dateIssued>2023-11</dateIssued>\n    </originInfo>\n    <typeOfResource>text</typeOfResource>\n    <relatedItem type=\"host\">\n        <titleInfo>\n            <title>Proceedings of the 13th International Joint Conference on Natural Language Processing and the 3rd Conference of the Asia-Pacific Chapter of the Association for Computational Linguistics: Tutorial Abstract</title>\n        </titleInfo>\n        <name type=\"personal\">\n            <namePart type=\"given\">Yun-Nung</namePart>\n            <namePart type=\"given\">(Vivian)</namePart>\n            <namePart type=\"family\">Chen</namePart>\n            <role>\n                <roleTerm authority=\"marcrelator\" type=\"text\">editor</roleTerm>\n            </role>\n        </name>\n        <name type=\"personal\">\n            <namePart type=\"given\">Sadao</namePart>\n            <namePart type=\"family\">Kurohashi</namePart>\n            <role>\n                <roleTerm authority=\"marcrelator\" type=\"text\">editor</roleTerm>\n            </role>\n        </name>\n        <originInfo>\n            <publisher>Association for Computational Linguistics</publisher>\n            <place>\n                <placeTerm type=\"text\">Nusa Dua, Bali</placeTerm>\n            </place>\n        </originInfo>\n        <genre authority=\"marcgt\">conference publication</genre>\n    </relatedItem>\n    <identifier type=\"citekey\">gala-etal-2023-developing</identifier>\n    <identifier type=\"doi\">10.18653/v1/2023.ijcnlp-tutorials.6</identifier>\n    <location>\n        <url>https://aclanthology.org/2023.ijcnlp-tutorials.6/</url>\n    </location>\n    <part>\n        <date>2023-11</date>\n        <extent unit=\"page\">\n            <start>35</start>\n            <end>42</end>\n        </extent>\n    </part>\n</mods>\n</modsCollection>\n\n```\n\nDownload as File Copy to Clipboard\n\n```\n%0 Conference Proceedings\n%T Developing State-Of-The-Art Massively Multilingual Machine Translation Systems for Related Languages\n%A Gala, Jay\n%A Chitale, Pra